                ALPHA SHATTERS SAP SD BENCHMARK RECORD

         
                 Dramatically outperforms competition
                  in business application environment
         
         
MAYNARD, Mass. -- January 2, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the highest-ever benchmark results for SAP's leading 
R/3 application suite. The benchmark achieved throughput of 210,384 
SAP transactions per hour with an average dialog response time of 
1.64 sec. A total of 1,700 SD benchmark users was measured, 
performing 525,960 dialog steps per hour. 

     Running on Digital's AlphaServer 8400 5/300 system with the 
Oracle7 database, the R/3 results demonstrate that the 64-bit 
Alpha symmetric multiprocessing platform (SMP) delivers to 
customers better performance and affordability than that of any 
other platform available today in SAP's widely accepted business 
application environment.
Benchmark Configuration

     A joint SAP/Digital/Oracle team measured the performance of 
the system using the standard SAP benchmark of the R/3 Sales & 
Distribution (SD) module at the Digital Technology Center in 
Walldorf, Germany. The benchmark environment was based on Digital 
UNIX V3.2C and Oracle V7.1.6.2.0 supporting SAP R/3 release 2.2D. 
This benchmark fully complies to SAP's recently issued stringent 
benchmark regulations and has been audited and certified by SAP.

     The client/server configuration included five 300MHz 
AlphaServer 8400 5/300 systems driven by the world's fastest and 
first BIPS (billion instructions per second) microprocessor -- the 
Alpha 21164. The database server was equipped with 10 CPUs (95 
percent CPU utilization) and 4 gigabytes (GB) of main memory. Four 
application servers employed 12 CPUs with 4 GB of main memory each, 
and one application server employed 4 CPUs and 4 GB of main memory. 
The benchmark fully utilized the available CPU capacity of the 
application servers.

     Further technical details and a benchmark report can be 
obtained from Digital.         

Alpha's Performance Advantage 

     The AlphaServer 8400 and 8200 enterprise servers deliver the 
industry's highest RISC performance and best price/performance for 
business-critical applications at one-tenth the price of the most 
widely used mainframes.

     Toni Steiner, Digital's director for SAP related business, 
said, "Once again, Digital has demonstrated its leading position in 
client/server computing. The AlphaServer 8400 SAP/Oracle benchmark 
results are far superior to any other platform tested so far. The 
tested equipment consists of proven products that are available 
today and are in daily productive use at numerous SAP customer 
sites," Steiner added.         

     In April, Digital and SAP announced record-setting host-based 
R/3 benchmark results. Today's client-server results place far 
greater demands on the entire system than do host-based 
implementations.         

     In early December, Digital provided added proof of Alpha's 
unique performance and price/performance advantages. Digital and 
Oracle announced a record-breaking TPC-C open systems benchmark, 
11,456 tpmC at $286/tpmC, far surpassing the existing performance 
record. The benchmark result dramatically demonstrates the combined 
power of the Oracle 64-bit very large memory option coupled with 
Digital's 64-bit UNIX and Alpha hardware architecture.         

     The December benchmark result came just six weeks after the 
Digital/Oracle ensemble shattered the then performance record. 
Commenting on that result, the Gartner Group wrote, "Digital 
confirmed and exceeded our expectations of industry leading UNIX 
server platform scaling, and provided long awaited confirmation of 
performance promises made by Oracle and Digital since the 8400's 
introduction last April. The performance ... helps substantiate 
scaling advantages from 64-bit addressing to very large physical 
memory space. Since larger main memory adds more cost, Digital's 
achievement of excelling in price/performance,... was equally 
impressive."

The Digital/SAP/Oracle Advantage         

     SAP provides flexible, integrated client/server and 
mainframe-based business applications software that is compatible 
with most popular hardware, software, and database platforms. SAP's 
R/3 client/server suite is installed in 4,300 customer sites 
worldwide and is accepted as the standard in key industries such as 
oil, chemicals, consumer packaged goods, and high 
technology/electronics. 

     The Oracle7 64-bit option enables businesses to run the 
database portion of applications such as data warehousing and 
online transaction processing more than 200 times faster than on 
current 32-bit enterprise systems. Commercial customers running 
decision support applications can extract vital information from 
mountains of data faster and more economically than ever before. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with 
industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace. 
