           DIGITAL INTRODUCES PENTIUM(R) 150MHz and 166MHz
        PROCESSORS ACROSS DESKTOP, RETAIL AND PC SERVER LINES


MAYNARD, Mass., January 4, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced its plans to incorporate the new 150MHz and 166MHz 
Intel(R) Pentium processors across its desktop, retail and server PC 
families.  Digital will include the new processors in several models 
within its Celebris XL, Celebris GL and Venturis commercial desktop 
families and is introducing two new powerful home computers in its 
Starion retail line.  The company also announced that it will offer 
166MHz Pentium-powered models of its award-winning Prioris server 
line in single- and dual-processor configurations.

     Pricing and volume shipment availability for the commercial 
desktop and server systems will be announced later this month.  
Digital's new Starion 950 and Starion 960 retail PCs are shipping 
now, at expected street prices of $2,999 and $3,199, respectively.  
Intel announced availability of the 150MHz and 166MHz Pentium 
processors earlier today.

     Digital's aggressive incorporation of the new Pentium 150MHz 
and 166MHz processors is part of its strategy to offer a wide range 
of competitively priced, highly reliable, feature-rich PCs with the 
latest technology advances.  Working with Intel, Microsoft and other 
technology partners enhances Digital's engineering excellence, 
overall design and best-of-breed componentry of its PCs. 
Digital has matched its own motherboard designs with Intel's 
microprocessor engineering to allow easy, streamlined integration of 
the new processors into its full PC family.  

     "Digital PC recognizes the importance of providing our 
customers the state-of-the-art in power, design and reliability, and 
continues to populate our PCs with the latest processors on the 
Intel Pentium power curve," said Howard Elias, vice president, 
Desktop and Mobile Product Lines for Digital's Personal Computer 
Business Unit.  Digital offers one of the broadest lines of Pentium 
PCs available -- designed for excellence and long-term value."

Celebris XL Personal Workstations:  "A Powerful 'Technical 
Workstation' in PC Clothing"

     Digital is adding the Celebris XL 5150 and Celebris XL 5166 
models and a dual-processor Celebris XL 5166 system to the 
industry's fastest personal workstation family, which includes 
models based on Intel Pentium, Pentium Pro (TM) and Digital Alpha 
processors, as well as certain components and options that are 
interchangeable between the three platforms.

     The Digital personal workstation's processor-independent 
architecture enables fast, smooth and easy migration to the latest 
Intel Pentium, Pentium Pro and Digital Alpha microprocessors, for 
long-term investment protection as customer's business needs change.  
Digital is offering its industry-leading PowerGrade program for 
166MHz processor upgrades -- users simply plug in the respective 
daughter cards. 

     Celebris XL models feature 16MB RAM, 256/512K cache, 1GB SCSI 
hard drive, Matrox Millennium graphics card, 4X CD-ROM, and 
Digital's ClientWORKS network and asset management software.

     In addition, AccelGraphics AG300 Graphics Adapters are now 
available for use on Pentium, Pentium Pro, and Alpha systems.  
Combined with Windows NT, Digital's personal workstation family 
provides users of technical and compute-intensive applications a 
combination of workstation-class performance and shrink-wrapped 
applications, with the look, feel and pricing of a PC.

Celebris GL PCs: Designed for Performance and Demanding Applications 

     Digital's award-winning Celebris GL PCs, designed from the 
start to be performance desktop systems, offer advanced business 
users a potent combination of performance, flexibility and 
ease-of-use, winning PC Magazine's December 1995 editor's choice 
award.  

     The new Celebris GL 5150 and Celebris GL 5166 models will be 
available in short-tower configurations.  Celebris GL systems are 
ideal for fast-response, demanding business and analytical 
applications, and feature integrated, best-of-breed componentry, 
including:  Pentium processors; EDO memory; pipeline burst cache; 
Intel Triton FX chipset; PCI bus master Enhanced-IDE and integrated, 
extended performance 64-bit graphics.  High-quality 16-bit stereo 
sound, quad-speed CD-ROM for fast response, and Digitals ClientWORKS 
software are included on preconfigured models.

Venturis PCs: Feature-Rich and Reliable for Enterprise Computing

     Digital brings the latest in Pentium power to its Venturis 
value line with the addition of the new Venturis 5150 and Venturis 
5166 systems, which will be available in both slimline and 
full-profile models. Venturis systems are designed to optimize 
productivity for enterprise computing users while offering exceptional 
price/performance.  Venturis systems are easy to use, service, and 
manage and also support Digital's ClientWORKS software.

Starion 950 and 960 PCs: Setting the Pace For Home Computing

     Digital is one of the first computer makers to ship retail PCs 
based on Intel's high-end processors for home and home-office 
computing.  Digital's new Starion 950 and 960 PCs combine the 
lightning speed of Intel Pentium 150MHz or 166MHz processors, the 
market's premier home-theater-quality sound, and top-of-the-line 
features aimed to please the cutting-edge consumer.

     With their high-powered Pentium processors, the new Starion 950 
and 960 have the muscle to run horsepower-hungry multimedia CDs and 
games.  They complete the multimedia experience with the Starion 
PC's unmatched sound system, treating consumers to the same clear 
highs and vibrant lows they experience in music and in movies.  The 
sound system features JBL satellite speakers, 16-bit audio with 
wavetable, and 3D surround sound.

     Starion 950 and 960 systems offer top-speed access to the 
Internet and popular online services with a 28.8 Kbps data/fax 
modem.  For managing home office or family communications needs, 
these full-featured models include a built-in answering machine with 
professional-quality voicemail and full-duplex, hands-free 
speakerphone.

     Like all current Starion PCs, these newest models sport a 
quad-speed CD-ROM drive, pre-loaded Windows 95, and a suite of 
best-selling home software, including popular Microsoft titles.

     Both the 150MHz-based Starion 950 and the 166MHz-based Starion 
960 come equipped with 16MB of memory, a large 1.6GB hard drive, and 
64-bit graphics.  They offer a choice of 15-inch (13.8-inch 
viewable) or 17-inch (15.8-inch viewable) SVGA flat-screen, 
anti-glare monitors.  Expected street prices for the monitors are 
$399 and $749, respectively.

     For the location of the nearest Starion retailer, call 
1-800-216-8115, or visit Digital on the World Wide Web at 
http://www.pc.digital.com

Prioris PC Servers: Scalability and Expandability for Maximum 
Investment Protection

     The Pentium 166MHz-powered server will be the latest addition 
to Digital's award-winning Prioris line of highly scalable, 
high-performance symmetric multiprocessing application servers for 
medium to large workgroups.  These PC servers are ideal for LAN 
consolidation and in environments where the highest degree of 
confidence in network integrity is mandatory.  In single- and 
dual-processor configurations, the Prioris HX family's balanced 
system design incorporates performance and expandability features, 
such as 512KB secondary level write-back cache, PCI Fast-Wide SCSI-2 
controllers and devices, and Digital's PCI-to-PCI bridge technology 
which provides a total of six bus-master PCI slots and six 
bus-master EISA slots.  As a result, the Prioris family matches 
high-speed processor technology with an enhanced throughput 
architecture to achieve maximum server performance.

     As with all current Prioris PC servers, Digital will include 
with the new systems -- at no extra cost -- Digital's ServerWORKS 
Manager, a software package that extends the capabilities of 
traditional server management to also provide critical network 
management functionality, and ServerWORKS Quick Launch, a CD-ROM 
suite of utilities that automates network operating system 
installation and the configuration of Digital Prioris PC servers.

     Full pricing and availability information will be released 
later this month.

World-Class Service and Support

     Digital's products are backed by a three-year limited hardware 
warranty and a worldwide service and support network.  The warranty 
includes one year of on-site service for desktop and retail PCs and 
three years for server products. (Note 1)  Digital has more than 
22,000 service professionals worldwide, including 800 Microsoft 
Certified professionals, and 5,000 support professionals trained on 
Microsoft products, including Windows, Windows 95, Windows NT, and a 
variety of other software products.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
                                ####

Note 1.  Digital monitors and Digital options are warranted 
separately. On-site service is available in most areas.  For desktop 
and retail products, some components in the first year of on-site 
service are covered under a customer-replaceable unit program.

