                     DIGITAL ANNOUNCES ENHANCED
                  INTERNET ALPHASERVER SOFTWARE KIT


  Everything in One Kit for Getting Real Business from the Internet


TORONTO, ON, CANADA (Internet World), January 10, 1995 -- Digital 
Equipment Corporation today announced the Internet AlphaServer 
Software Kit for Digital UNIX V.2. This enhancement of Digital's 
proven Internet AlphaServer Software Kit brings customers everything 
they need to make their site internet-application ready. Digital 
has consolidated, compiled, tested and integrated all the software 
in the Kit for interoperability so that users can save time and 
money when they set up and install their system.

     Improved features include graphical Internet AlphaServer 
administration software scripts for quick installation and a 
graphical interface for setup and management of Internet news 
groups. Digital's AlphaServer system can handle thousands of 
Internet newsgroups on one server. The Kit also includes 
tcpwrapper, an enhanced Internet security application that allows 
users to turn off certain programs that expose systems to unsecured 
Internet traffic, as well as a test to verify changes. The enhanced 
Software Kit can now run in Digital's DECsafe Available Server 
Environment (ASE), allowing users access to their web site even if a 
failure occurs.  

     "The Net is today's hot spot for doing business. No company 
can afford to ignore the business implications of representation on 
the Internet. It's the global vehicle for expanding users markets, 
taking offerings worldwide and laying a strong foundation for future 
commerce," said Rose Ann Giordano, vice president of Digital's 
Internet Business Group.

     Unique among UNIX versions, the 64-bit Digital UNIX 
architecture can support 1,000 simultaneous domain names, enabling 
Internet Service Providers to host multiple customer sites on one 
server. The Internet AlphaServer Software Kit runs in all models of 
Digital's powerful AlphaServer family. The kit is also prepackaged 
on two new AlphaServer systems including the 1000/266 and 400/233. 
The Internet AlphaServer kit brings customers everything they need 
to make their site Internet-application ready.

     Giordano continued, "With the enhanced Internet AlphaServer 
Software Kit, Digital has again assembled useful, feature-rich, 
robust versions of popular public and supported Internet 
applications. The kit helps users get their Web site up and running 
in time to obtain real results in today's virtual marketplace. The 
continuous improvements to the Kit are based on customer feedback, 
the transition of the Internet from pilot systems to production 
systems and customers need for 64-bit Alpha performance."

The new version of the software kit adds the following features and 
functionality:

     o	 Ease of installation and management--Scripts that easily 
         guide the user through the installation process, saving  
         time and getting servers up and running faster. Graphical 
         scripts also facilitate management.

     o	 Applications--all the applications needed to do business 
     	 on the Internet including Mail, news, web serving, proxy   
         caching for fast customer response, Netscape 
         Communications' industry leading server software and more.

     o	 Enhanced Internet security--provided with the inclusion of 
         tcpwrapper. This program allows users to turn off programs 
         such as remote login, file transfer (FTP), telnet, and mail 
         which expose systems to unsecured Internet traffic.

     o	 Scalability--From entry-level to full enterprise-wide 	    
         production systems. Users can use the Internet kit on the  
         Digital system that meets their current application needs, 
         then expand as requirements increase. 

     o	 Worldwide service and support--service and support from    
         over 450  locations in more than 100 countries worldwide to 
         keep customers on the Net, continuously and cost-
     	 effectively.

     o	 High availability--for Internet-accessed information 	    
         repositories, hosting home pages, or use in electronic     
         commerce.  The  optional DECsafe application functionality 
         is particularly important to Internet sites with large     
         populations and high availability needs. 

     o	 High performance--Digital's industry-leading 64-bit Alpha  
         architecture and 64-bit UNIX operating system provide 	    
         unmatched performance right where users need it--in front  
         of millions of customers, 24 hours a day.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
