            DIGITAL AND MICROSOFT SOFTIMAGE TEAM TO OFFER
          UNPRECEDENTED PRICE/PERFORMANCE FOR HIGH-END 3-D
                    WINDOWS NT ANIMATION SOFTWARE


  Softimage 3D for Windows NT on Alpha Workstations provides record
     breaking performance at only half the previous system cost

    
MAYNARD, Mass., January 16, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that Microsoft's award-winning three dimensional 
modeling and animation software, Softimage 3D, is now available for 
the Windows NT operating system running on Alpha workstations.  This 
combination of hardware and software provides the same production-
proven 3-D animation environment previously available only on UNIX-
based workstations from Silicon Graphics, and at approximately half 
the system cost.  

     Softimage 3D for Windows NT, announced today by Microsoft, is 
available now on the Alpha XL 266 Personal Workstation and the 
AlphaStation 600 Model 5/266.  Digital is one of three system 
vendors chosen to partner with Microsoft on this offering, and the 
only one offering the record breaking speed of Alpha 
microprocessors.  In recently conducted rendering tests, Digital's 
AlphaStation 600 Model 5/266 running Softimage 3D outperformed the 
Silicon Graphics Indigo II Extreme workstation by a factor of 1.5.

     "Digital's Alpha hardware and the Windows NT operating system 
are combining once again to expand the marketplace by bringing 
leadership technology to unheard of price/performance points", said 
Lucia Quinn, vice president for Digital's Windows NT Business 
Segment.  "We've lowered the cost of entry by offering economically 
priced hardware running powerful applications that provide the kind 
of no compromise performance that has previously been available only 
on high priced UNIX workstations."

     Both the Alpha XL 266 and the AlphaStation 600 5/266 come fully 
bundled with Softimage 3D for Windows NT, 20" multisynch color 
monitor, ZLP-L1 3D high-end OpenGL graphics, 2 GB disk, and a choice 
of 64MB or 128MB of memory.  Pricing ranges from $17,995 for the 
Alpha XL 266 with 64MB to $27,995 for the AlphaStation 600 5/266 
with 128MB of memory.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Intel and Alpha 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace. 
