           PMDF e-Mail Interconnect products augment and complement
         Digital's Enterprise Messaging solutions with SMTP/MIME and
                          PC LAN mailer connectivity

 
        DIGITAL TO RESELL INNOSOFT INTERNATIONAL'S PRODUCTS WORLDWIDE
 

Melbourne, Australia -- 30 January 1996 -- Digital Equipment 
Corporation and Innosoft International, Inc. have signed a 
worldwide agreement under which Digital will resell PMDF e-Mail 
Interconnect software products. 

     PMDF products from Innosoft have historically provided SMTP 
(Simple Mail Transport Protocol) support for Digital's VMS Mail and
Message Router environments including ALL-IN-1. 

     Digital is the worldwide leader in multivendor Enterprise 
Messaging integration. With a network of hundreds of messaging 
consultants and experts, and more than 25 dedicated messaging 
solution teams, Digital provides integrated hardware, software, 
planning, worldwide implementation and support for its customers' 
messaging needs.

     In May 1992, PMDF was enhanced and shipped as the first 
commercial software product to support the then-new MIME 
(Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions) specification. By using 
MIME as the standard format throughout the product set, PMDF is 
able to handle all of the standard and non-standard message formats
utilised by other mail systems, including binary attachments. 

     PMDF products provide tightly integrated connectivity for
MAILbus 400 MTA's to SMTP/MIME environments such as the Internet
and to all of the major PC LAN mail systems including Microsoft
Mail, Lotus cc:Mail, GroupWise, and Novell MHS-based mailers. 

     Equally important to many of Digital's existing customers, PMDF 
products continue to provide seamless support for ALL-IN-1 users 
migrating to new messaging environments being implemented, 
including MAILbus 400 and Microsoft Exchange.

     "Our formal business agreement with Innosoft that will
facilitate 'one stop shopping' from Digital for our customers
implementing comprehensive messaging solutions," said Avi Corfas,
worldwide director for electronic commerce at Digital. 

     "PMDF products have been tightly integrated with Digital 
technology for years. Customers buying them through Digital will 
gain the same support we give our products," he said.

     "Innosoft and its authorised PMDF distributors worldwide look 
forward to working even more closely with Digital in providing 
fully integrated and comprehensive enterprise messaging solutions 
to the market," said Clyde Johnston, president of Innosoft. 

     "We have been shipping PMDF products exclusively on Digital 
platforms since 1987, and our special expertise involves bringing 
'Internet-style' technology to the task of integrating multiple, 
disparate, often legacy, and sometimes proprietary mail systems. 

     "Any organisation with serious messaging requirements needs 
standards-based native support for both X.400 and Internet 
technologies, and the Digital/Innosoft combination will be 
delivering world class competence on both fronts."

     Digital's three-tier client/server architecture, based on X.400 
and SMTP, incorporates Digital and partner software running on 
Intel and Digital's Alpha 64-bit UNIX and OpenVMS platforms, 
consulting, implementation, support and operation services for the
most demanding enterprise messaging applications.

     Through the Alliance for Enterprise Computing, Digital is the 
world's leading provider of Enterprise Messaging solutions based on
Microsoft exchange.

     Innosoft's PMDF product line runs on the same three platforms
to complement and augment the overall Digital solution, thus 
facilitating very tight integration. In addition to SMTP/MIME 
Internet connectivity, the PMDF product set provides for 
integration and support of other Digital messaging systems, PC LAN
mail systems, and many other messaging environments. 

     Innosoft International, Inc., headquartered in West Covina, 
California, develops and markets "Internet-style" e-mail 
integration software products, exclusively for Digital customers, 
both directly to end users, and through a network of international
distributors. 

     PMDF products are presently installed at more than 1,900 sites
in 46 countries throughout the world. Innosoft's high rate of
growth has earned placement on the "Inc." magazine listings of the
500 fastest growing private companies in the United States for both 
1994 and 1995.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms,
storage, networking, software and services, together with
industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organisations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
