                 DIGITAL ANNOUNCES PRIORIS ZX 5133MP
                     HIGH-PERFORMANCE PC SERVER


  Announces New Pentium Models of Prioris HX, LX and XL PC Servers


MAYNARD, Mass., January 30, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the Prioris ZX 5133MP superserver, the premier 
product in a new line of Symmetric Multiprocessing (SMP) enterprise 
PC servers that will carry the "ZX" designation.  Based on the 
133MHz Pentium microprocessor, the Prioris ZX 5133MP is targeted at 
enterprise-class applications that require the highest level of 
performance and reliability.  The company also announced the 
immediate availability of new Pentium processor models of the 
Prioris LX, Prioris XL Server and Prioris HX PC servers.

     "While raw system performance is a always a significant factor 
-- especially in the enterprise server area -- high-end PC 
superservers such as our ZX series must be augmented with new 
technologies and industry-standard software solutions that improve 
their manageability, fault-resilience and ease-of-use," said Duane 
Dickhut, vice president of Digital's PC server product line.  
"Digital's unrivaled expertise in Windows NT clustering and advanced 
database technology, as well as our roster of strategic partnerships 
with industry leaders such as Microsoft, Novell and Oracle, has 
uniquely positioned our company to lead the way in Intel-based 
enterprise computing."

     The newest addition to Digital's award-winning Intel server 
family, the Prioris ZX 5133MP is a high-performance, high-
availability, scalable superserver for resource-intensive 
applications such as database transaction processing, decision 
support,  groupware, internet access, and general file and print or 
e-mail services for large LANs.  The Prioris ZX is optimized as a 
robust line-of-business application server ideal for large branch 
offices and remote sites in a variety of industries including 
financial services, retail, manufacturing, transportation, 
communications and government, and for organizations migrating to a 
client/server environment using Windows NT or UNIX.

     The new server incorporates Intel's industry-standard 
Multi-processing Specification (MPS 1.1 or 1.4) and supports SMP 
scalability from one to four 133MHz Pentium processors.  Each CPU is 
equipped with up to one MB of dedicated secondary level, two-way 
write-back cache for maximum performance in database-intensive 
applications.  Extending Digital's leadership position in PCI 
technology, the new system features a state-of-the-art dual peer PCI 
bus and integrated dual Fast/Wide SCSI controllers to provide 
maximum throughput for heavy file sharing and database-intensive 
tasks.  As with all of Digital's Prioris PC servers, the Prioris ZX 
5133MP delivers maximum investment longevity through balanced system 
design, a highly expandable architecture and robust fault-tolerance.

Enterprise Application ISV Partnerships

     To complement its world-class hardware offerings, Digital is 
working closely with key ISVs to offer customers complete server and 
software solutions for critical applications that best exploit the 
Prioris ZX 5133MP server's unique abilities in enterprise-class 
applications. Among these network operating system and applications 
partners are Lotus, Microsoft, Novell, Oracle and SCO.  Specific 
distribution arrangements and solution set availability will be 
announced throughout early 1996.

     In addition, the Prioris ZX 5133MP is currently engaged in the 
SAP/R3 certification process and the company continues its 
leadership in developing Windows NT clustering solutions by 
leveraging its own engineering expertise and experience, as well as 
its cooperative work with Microsoft.
 
Scalability, Expandability, Manageability, Compatibility

     The Prioris ZX PC server provides the power and throughput to 
tackle the most demanding server applications through expandable 
processor, disk, memory and I/O subsystems, as well as optional 
advanced RAID configurations. This flexibility helps protect 
customers' technology investments as demand multimedia database and 
high-traffic Internet applications become more prevalent. Digital's 
new superserver comes standard with ECC memory and a maximum memory 
capacity of 768MB.  The new system also features nine total 
bus-master I/O slots (five PCI for maximum performance, four EISA 
for legacy card compatibility); up to 28GB internal storage capacity 
with external support for up to one terabyte; 11 total drive bays 
including seven hot-swappable bays; optional redundant power supply, 
standard redundant cooling and a rackmount-ready chassis.

     Like all Prioris PC servers, each Prioris ZX 5133MP superserver 
will include --  at no extra cost -- Digital's ServerWORKS Manager, 
an easy-to-use server and network management software package, and 
ServerWORKS Quick Launch, a CD-ROM suite of utilities that automates 
network operating system installation and the configuration of 
Digital Prioris PC servers.  Digital's Remote Server Manager option 
provides out-of-band server management and control for remote or 
distributed sites with limited on-site LAN administration capabilities.  
In addition, Digital's rackmount option allows any combination of 
Prioris servers and external storage devices to be installed in a rack 
without modification to the systems' chassis or wiring.

Prioris ZX 5133MP Pricing and Availability

     The Prioris ZX 5133MP family will be available on February 12, 
1996. A Prioris ZX 5133MP/1 RAID system equipped with a single 
Pentium 133MHz processor, 512KB of synchronous secondary two-way 
write-back cache, a dual-channel PCI RAID controller, 32MB of memory 
with two-way interleaving, integrated dual Fast/Wide SCSI-2 
controllers, a quad-speed CD-ROM drive, and three 2.1GB SCSI hard 
disk drives carries a suggested list price of $17,119.  

     A Prioris ZX 5133MP/2 RAID system equipped with dual symmetric 
multiprocessing Pentium 133MHz processors, 1MB of synchronous 
secondary two-way write-back cache per processor, a dual-channel PCI 
RAID controller, 64MB of memory with two-way interleaving, 
integrated dual Fast/Wide SCSI-2 controllers, a quad-speed CD-ROM 
drive, and three 2.1GB SCSI hard disk drives carries a suggested 
list price of $24,369.

     The Prioris ZX 5133MP family is upgradeable in one- and 
two-processor increments.  A one-processor upgrade card with 512KB 
of synchronous secondary two-way write-back cache carries a 
suggested list price of $6,249. A two-processor upgrade card with 
1MB of synchronous secondary two-way write-back cache per processor 
carries a suggested list price of $12,429.  A second memory card 
upgrade is priced at $359.

     The Prioris ZX 5133MP superserver is certified with a wide 
range of operating systems, including Windows NT Server 3.51; Novell 
NetWare 3.X , 4.X, and NetWare SMP; SCO UnixWare; SCO Open Server 
5.0; IBM OS/2 SMP; and Banyan VINES.

New Prioris Pentium Processor Choices for HX, LX and XL Server

     The Prioris HX 5166 is Digital's latest addition to its 
award-winning Prioris HX family of scalable Pentium-powered 
symmetric multiprocessing PC servers.  In single- and dual-processor 
configurations, the Prioris HX 5166 server's balanced system design 
integrates high-performance and expandability features such as 512KB 
secondary level write-back cache (standard), PCI Fast-Wide SCSI-2 
controllers and devices, and Digital's PCI-to-PCI bridge technology 
for a total of six bus-master PCI slots and six bus-master EISA 
slots. Digital's Prioris HX 5166 system is a superior departmental 
server for medium to large workgroups and is ideal for LAN 
consolidation and for environments where the highest degree of 
reliability is mandatory.  

     Digital also announced today new Pentium processor models of 
the Prioris LX, the company's reliable, easy-to-manage and highly 
integrated entry-level server, and of the Prioris XL Server, a 
flexible, expandable general purpose file server.  The Prioris LX 
5120 and the Prioris XL Server 5133 offer the latest in proven 
high-performance Pentium processor technology to provide customers 
with the best return on their client/server investments. 

Prioris HX 5166, XL Server 5133 and LX 5120 Pricing and Availability

     A Prioris HX 5166 RAID system equipped with a single Pentium 
166MHz processor, 16MB of parity memory, 512KB secondary level 
write-back cache, a Cirrus Logic 5428 video controller, a two 
channel  PCI RAID controller, and two 2GB SCSI hard disk drives 
carries a suggested list price of $13,119.  An identically equipped 
system with 32MB of ECC memory is priced at $15,193.

     A Prioris HX 5166DP RAID system equipped with dual Pentium 
166MHz processors, 32MB of ECC memory, 512KB secondary level 
write-back cache, a Cirrus Logic 5428 video controller, a two 
channel  PCI RAID controller, and four 2GB SCSI hard disk drives 
carries a suggested list price of $26,441. All members of the 
Prioris HX 5166 family are available immediately.

     A Prioris LX 5120 equipped with a single 120MHz Pentium 
processor, 16MB of parity memory, 256KB of secondary write-back 
cache, one 1GB SCSI hard disk drive, one, quad-speed CD-ROM drive, 
an Adaptec 7850 narrow SCSI controller and an on-board Cirrus 5428 
video controller carries a suggested list price of $3,889 and is 
available immediately.

     A Prioris XL Server 5133 equipped with a single 133MHz Pentium 
processor, 16MB of parity memory, 256KB of secondary write-back 
cache, one 1GB SCSI hard disk drive, one quad-speed CD-ROM drive, an 
Adaptec 7850 Fast/Wide SCSI controller and an on-board Cirrus Logic 
5428 video controller carries a suggested list price of $4,759 and 
is available immediately.

     A Prioris XL Server 5133DP equipped with two symmetrical 
multiprocessing 133MHz Pentium processors, 32MB of parity memory, 
512KB of secondary write-back cache, one 1GB SCSI hard disk drive, 
one quad-speed CD-ROM drive, an Adaptec 7850 Fast/Wide SCSI 
controller and an on-board Cirrus 5428 video controller carries a 
suggested list price of $6,699 and is available immediately.

     Digital's Prioris PC servers are covered by a standard 
three-year, on-site limited warranty, with next-business day 
response standard (in most locations) from Digital's Multivendor 
Customer Services organization or an authorized Digital Warranty 
Service Provider.  Prioris servers are available through Digital's 
channel partners including master resellers, wholesalers, 
distributors, dealers, VARs and system integrators.  

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with 
industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in todays global marketplace.
